<title>USA: Ahmanson spent $74.7 mln to buyback shares.</title>
<headline>Ahmanson spent $74.7 mln to buyback shares.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>H.F. Ahmanson and Co on Friday said it spent $74.7 million to buy back 1.97 million shares of its own stock from March 26 to May 27.</p>
<p>It said it expected to receive Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) approval soon for an exchange offer for Great Western.</p>
<p>The company is required to end its repurchase program once it launches the exchange program, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Ahmanson launched a hostile bid for Great Western in February. Great Western has rejected the offer and agreed instead to merge with Washington Mutual Inc.</p>
<p>Great Western shareholders are set to vote on the merger with Washington Mutual on June 13.</p>
</text>
